really striking all right republican  congressman mike gallagher of wisconsin  condemned the president and his  supporters before and  after yesterday's riot at capitol hill  he joins us now congressman good morning  thank you so much for being with us good  morning  what was your experience like yesterday  on the floor when all of this broke out  well it all uh spiraled out of control  very quickly  i was in my office and you started  hearing flashbangs in the distance which  was presumably  the capitol police trying to get the  rioters to step back and the rioters  violently confronted them and somehow  breached the security perimeter of the  capitol  and all of a sudden were running around  statuary hall  the vice president was rushed off the  floor of the house of representatives by  secret service and  these images started to emerge as the  the you know  the flashbangs continued of the house  floor being barricaded windows broken i  mean the whole thing  was absolute chaos it was not something  i thought i would ever see  in the united states capital so it was a  very dark day it was very concerning day  i was very concerned for  a lot of my colleagues and i found  myself barricaded in my own office  with a couple of my staff members  thinking about you know how do we if the  worst comes to worst how do we  how do we keep this office safe how do i  keep my staff safe and it was just  you know it was a very very dark day did  you feel like your life was  in danger at some point no i never felt  that  i mean i but i was you know i was  thinking that the closest  thing this resembled was some things i  saw in iraq when i  served in uniform over a decade ago i  mean it was just that  chaotic but i never really felt that my  life was in danger but when the images  started to emerge i thought that some of  my colleagues who were on the house  floor at the time  their life could be in danger and then  ultimately tragically  um a woman was shot and she lost her  life and my understanding is the death  toll is that  four now so it's absolutely tragic and i  think we have to confront head on the  fact that there  was a real danger to giving  millions of americans false hope that  somehow  congress was going to overturn the  results  of the election on january 6. i mean my  view is that congress that is not our  role constitutionally it's for the  states and the people  to resolve their own elections january 6  has always been merely a ministerial  meeting  of congress not a meaningful forum for  litigating or relitigating an election  and i think what the objectors  misunderstood is that somehow by just  having a debate for two hours  the protesters were going to be  satisfied  well clearly that was not the case and  we incited some very extreme passions  and that  resulted in destruction and even death  extreme passions indeed congressman  gallagher and let's talk about that for  a second because considering what  everybody had gone through that day  and how traumatic and upsetting it was  that several of your republican  colleagues  still continue to voice their objections  what did you think about that  well i thought clearly after what we  watched happen for hours  of utter destruction that we would  reconvene  and the objectors would drop their  objections  yes a lot of people they went right back  to  the debate they went right back to the  reckless  suggestion that congress had a role in  overturning the election on january 6th  so  i was quite frankly astounded at that uh  i was astounded that there wasn't a  movement from the top down to prevent  that from happening i guess  i was gratified that the number of  senators who were going to object  was reduced to a very small number and  perhaps we objected to a fewer number of  states than we originally were but  i i just don't understand how after  witnessing what we witnessed  and knowing knowing that  congressman mike gallagher thank you so  much for being with you with us this  morning we're glad you're okay we're  glad everyone's okay  i'm glad the country's okay
 

